# Angular Modern Practices

- Use current Angular APIs and avoid deprecated or outdated syntax and lifecycle patterns.
- Prefer standalone components, typed reactive forms, and signal-friendly patterns where applicable.
- Keep business logic in services/facades; keep components focused on presentation and orchestration.
- Use `OnPush` change detection for performance-sensitive components by default.
- Keep templates simple: move complex expressions into computed properties or methods.
- Manage subscriptions safely (`async` pipe, `takeUntilDestroyed`, or framework-recommended patterns).
- Ensure route-level boundaries are lazy-loaded when it improves startup performance.
- Keep Angular code aligned with ESLint, strict TypeScript checks, and framework style guidance.
